  "result_semantics": "Result declarations bind the committed action payload in Operation.result_handle; they do not advertise implementation or native qualification. Receipt-only actions report through Operation and never carry a payload handle. Schema and selected-adapter actions require a complete retrievable result before succeeded, including an empty typed output where that method permits it. The receiving owner atomically retains exact result bytes, installed schema identity and Operation result binding before acknowledging terminal success. A completed native effect without required result custody remains unresolved with its effects and holds preserved. Pending, failed, cancelled and quarantined records may have null results; a retained result never implies success by itself. Schema actions bind the listed closed schema and installed transitive schema closure. adapter.execute binds its exact approved selected method result schema in the reviewed subject. Complete bytes and their independently installed exact schema must verify before consumption. Qualified recovery readers may support an exact prior schema closure without rewriting accepted output or granting new execution authority."
